  "limitations": [
    "Real-network loading uses the configured client HTTPS proxy, actual public origin resources and fresh browser contexts. Touch/network/CPU conditions are emulated, not physical phone measurements.",
    "The first public measurement run was interrupted after three completed cases because the SSH deployment connection had disconnected. Fresh inspection confirmed cutover had completed and both services were healthy; completed slow measurements are retained.",
    "Desktop cold visits varied from 17.817 to 77.556 seconds. This is substantial variance, not a p95 or a stable speed guarantee. Downloading remains a bottleneck.",
    "The client/server clock skew is about eight hours. New fingerprinted immutable resources remain fresh; do not generalize old one-hour-cache repeat timing to synchronized clients. Conditional 304 and decoded/encoded bytes were checked independently.",
    "First-race timing includes the deferred car/combat preparation and countdown. It is reported to avoid hiding work behind an early menu. Optional media can abort/reissue streaming ranges; those events are retained separately from page/asset errors.",
    "Runtime FPS uses verified cached assets and real native API on Intel Iris Xe. It measures one 20-second auto-quality Harbour case, not cold-network startup or all-map/device performance.",
    "Four catalog/UI tests fail identically on the unmodified public platform baseline. They are recorded separately from the passing transport suites; publisher and discovery semantics were not changed."
  ],
